      "type": "model",
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Let me work through the mathematics carefully.\n\n**Part (1):** Given $\\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{n} = \\dfrac{a_n}{n+1} + \\dfrac{1}{n(n+1)}$.\n\nMultiply both sides by $n(n+1)$:\n$$(n+1)a_{n+1} = n a_n + 1$$\n\nSo $(n+1)a_{n+1} - n a_n = 1$, a constant. Let $b_n = n a_n$. Then $b_{n+1} - b_n = 1$, so $\\{n a_n\\}$ is an arithmetic sequence with common difference 1.\n\nWith $b_1 = 1\\cdot a_1 = 3$, we get $b_n = n a_n = 3 + (n-1)\\cdot 1 = n+2$, hence $a_n = \\dfrac{n+2}{n}$.\n\n**Part (2):** $f(x) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} a_k x^k = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} \\dfrac{k+2}{k} x^k = \\sum_{k=1}^{m}\\left(1 + \\dfrac{2}{k}\\right)x^k$.\n\n$f'(x) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} (k+2) x^{k-1}$.\n\nSo $f'(-2) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} (k+2)(-2)^{k-1}$.\n\nLet $S = \\sum_{k=1}^{m}(k+2)(-2)^{k-1}$. Write $k+2 = (k+1)+1$:\n$$S = \\sum_{k=1}^{m}(k+1)(-2)^{k-1} + \\sum_{k=1}^{m}(-2)^{k-1}$$\n\nNote $\\sum_{k=1}^{m}(k+1)(-2)^{k-1} = \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sum_{k=1}^{m} x^{k+1}\\right]_{x=-2} = \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{x^2(x^m-1)}{x-1}\\right]_{x=-2}$.\n\nLet me compute directly. Let $T = \\sum_{k=1}^{m}(k+1)r^{k-1}$ with $r=-2$. Using $\\sum_{k=1}^{m} k r^{k-1} = \\frac{1-(m+1)r^m + m r^{m+1}}{(1-r)^2}$ and $\\sum_{k=1}^m r^{k-1} = \\frac{1-r^m}{1-r}$.\n\nWith $r=-2$, $1-r=3$, $(1-r)^2=9$:\n- $\\sum_{k=1}^m k(-2)^{k-1} = \\frac{1-(m+1)(-2)^m + m(-2)^{m+1}}{9}$\n- $\\sum_{k=1}^m (-2)^{k-1} = \\frac{1-(-2)^m}{3}$\n\n$T = \\sum (k+1)(-2)^{k-1} = \\sum k(-2)^{k-1} + \\sum (-2)^{k-1} = \\frac{1-(m+1)(-2)^m + m(-2)^{m+1}}{9} + \\frac{1-(-2)^m}{3}$\n\n$= \\frac{1-(m+1)(-2)^m + m(-2)^{m+1} + 3 - 3(-2)^m}{9} = \\frac{4 - (m+4)(-2)^m + m(-2)^{m+1}}{9}$\n\nSince $(-2)^{m+1} = -2(-2)^m$: $= \\frac{4 - (m+4)(-2)^m - 2m(-2)^m}{9} = \\frac{4 - (3m+4)(-2)^m}{9}$\n\nThen $S = T + \\frac{1-(-2)^m}{3} = \\frac{4-(3m+4)(-2)^m}{9} + \\frac{3-3(-2)^m}{9} = \\frac{7 - (3m+7)(-2)^m}{9}$.\n\nLet me verify with $m=1$: $S$ should be $(1+2)(-2)^0 = 3$. Formula: $\\frac{7-(3+7)(-2)}{9} = \\frac{7+20}{9}=3$. ✓\n\n$m=2$: $3 + 4(-2) = 3-8=-5$. Formula: $\\frac{7-(6+7)\\cdot 4}{9}=\\frac{7-52}{9}=\\frac{-45}{9}=-5$. ✓",
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "call_efbfb8807316437a806af190",
            "index": 0,
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "submit_solution",
              "arguments": "{\"region_id\": \"region_art_0013_01\", \"final_answer\": \"（1）{n a_n} 是首项为 3、公差为 1 的等差数列，故 n a_n = n+2，即 a_n = (n+2)/n。\\n（2）f′(−2) = [7 − (3m+7)(−2)^m] / 9。\", \"reasoning\": \"【第(1)问】已知 a_1=3，且 a_{n+1}/n = a_n/(n+1) + 1/[n(n+1)]。\\n两边同乘 n(n+1)（n≥1）得：\\n(n+1)a_{n+1} = n a_n + 1，即 (n+1)a_{n+1} − n a_n = 1。\\n令 b_n = n a_n，则 b_{n+1} − b_n = 1 为常数，所以 {b_n}={n a_n} 是等差数列，公差 d=1。\\n首项 b_1 = 1·a_1 = 3，故 b_n = n a_n = 3 + (n−1)·1 = n+2，从而 a_n = (n+2)/n = 1 + 2/n。\\n\\n【第(2)问】由 a_k = (k+2)/k 得\\nf(x) = Σ_{k=1}^{m} a_k x^k = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+2)/k · x^k = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (1 + 2/k) x^k。\\n求导：f′(x) = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+2) x^{k−1}。\\n代入 x=−2：f′(−2) = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+2)(−2)^{k−1}。\\n记 S = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+2)(−2)^{k−1}，把 k+2 拆成 (k+1)+1：\\nS = Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+1)(−2)^{k−1} + Σ_{k=1}^{m} (−2)^{k−1}。\\n利用等比数列求和公式 Σ_{k=1}^{m} r^{k−1} = (1−r^m)/(1−r) 及 Σ_{k=1}^{m} k r^{k−1} = [1−(m+1)r^m + m r^{m+1}]/(1−r)^2，取 r=−2（1−r=3，(1−r)^2=9）：\\nΣ_{k=1}^{m} k(−2)^{k−1} = [1−(m+1)(−2)^m + m(−2)^{m+1}]/9，\\nΣ_{k=1}^{m} (−2)^{k−1} = [1−(−2)^m]/3。\\n于是 Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k+1)(−2)^{k−1} = [4 − (3m+4)(−2)^m]/9（用到 (−2)^{m+1} = −2(−2)^m）。\\n故 S = [4 − (3m+4)(−2)^m]/9 + [1−(−2)^m]/3 = [7 − (3m+7)(−2)^m]/9。\\n检验：m=1 时 S=3，公式给 (7+20)/9=3；m=2 时 S=3−8=−5，公式给 (7−52)/9=−5，均吻合。\\n所以 f′(−2) = [7 − (3m+7)(−2)^m]/9。\"}"
